# OIDC resource-server JWT verification

Generated by `ddd recipe oidc-resource-server --path <service> --dry-run`, then
the same command without `--dry-run`. Dry-run writes nothing. Conflicting files
abort before writes; identical reruns leave files alone. No module is auto-wired.
Install `jose@^6.2.12` explicitly with the service's approved package workflow.

Import `OidcResourceServerModule.register({ issuer, jwksUri, audiences,
authorizedClients, algorithms, clockToleranceSeconds: 0 })` in the owning module;
inject `OidcAccessTokenVerifier` and call `verify(originalAccessToken)`.
All URLs must be explicitly trusted HTTPS URLs from deployment configuration,
never request data. Audiences are resource/project audiences, not automatically
browser client IDs. Client allowlisting reads the issuer's `azp` claim.

Only asymmetric algorithms are accepted. Signature, issuer, resource audience,
authorized client, nonempty subject, finite required exp/iat and optional nbf
are checked. Clock skew is bounded to 0..60 seconds. JWKS failure fails closed;
the remote key cache is not a user/permission or token-revocation cache.

This verifies a JWT, not universal proof that it is an access token. Issuers
can issue ID and access tokens with overlapping signed claims. The consumer
MUST enforce its selected provider access-token profile and current actor
validation before granting access. A valid ID token is never an API credential.
Do not map returned roles/groups to product permissions implicitly. HUMAN versus
machine, current organization, canonical identity binding, staff membership,
revocation and transactional authorization belong to the consuming service.

Compatibility: jose v6 is maintained ESM. CommonJS consumers require Node
20.19+, 22.12+ or 23+ with require(esm), or Bun. Node 22.22 and Nest 11 are the
target baseline. Jest's VM module loader is distinct from native Node: execute
the generated CommonJS crypto test in a subprocess, not with a mocked verifier.
Do not downgrade to an unmaintained jose major to satisfy a test loader.

Primary references checked 2026-09-12:
https://github.com/panva/jose (supported runtimes, require(esm), security policy)
https://github.com/panva/jose/blob/main/docs/jwt/verify/functions/jwtVerify.md
